B.F1=s(["Keeping two services in agreement about who a user is, using one token instead of two login systems.","Modelling many-to-many membership with admin rules for joining, leaving and inviting.","Tracking read state per user per message without bloating the messages table.","Testing HTTP and socket flows before a client existed, using Insomnia against every endpoint."],t.s)
B.zd=new A.oI("Chat needs durable relational data (accounts, memberships, history) and instant delivery. Forcing one framework to do both well usually means compromising on one of them.","Split the responsibilities. Laravel owns authentication, the schema and every database write through a REST API. A Node.js server running Socket.IO owns the live connections and fans messages out to chat members.","Clients sign in against the Laravel API and receive a bearer token. The same token identifies them to the Node gateway, which pushes new messages to the other members of that chat. Five tables model it: users, chats, a chat_user pivot for membership, messages, and messages_read for read receipts.",B.F1,"Designing the schema and REST contract first, and proving it in Insomnia before adding sockets, keeps the real-time layer thin. Persistence and delivery are different jobs, and separating them made each easier to reason about.")
B.E3=s([u.E],t.s)
B.ze=new A.oI("Bored?.","TETRIS.","1 screen, falling blocks, higher scres .",B.E3,"I blow at this game.")
B.DC=s(["Implementing reliable offline-first sync without data conflicts when the device reconnects.","Parsing unstructured OCR text from lab reports with varying formats across different labs.","Generating pixel-perfect PDF reports that render consistently across Android, iOS, and web.","Securing health data in transit and at rest while maintaining fast load times."],t.s)
B.zf=new A.oI("Patients with chronic conditions struggle to keep track of lab results across multiple visits and providers. Paper records get lost, digital portals are fragmented, and most apps require constant internet access \u2014 a real barrier in areas with poor connectivity.","ChroniCare unifies health tracking, lab result scanning, and report generation in one cross-platform app. A FastAPI OCR microservice extracts structured data from photographed lab reports, while an Express/Node backend handles authentication and persistent storage. A local-first architecture ensures the app works fully offline.","Flutter frontend communicates with an Express/Node API via Dio. BLoC manages all state transitions. A separate FastAPI microservice handles OCR processing using Tesseract. Prisma ORM connects to the database. Offline data is persisted locally and synced via a background queue when connectivity resumes.",B.DC,"Building offline-first from day one is far easier than retrofitting it. Defining a clear sync conflict resolution strategy early saved significant debugging time. The OCR service taught me the value of microservices \u2014 isolating it meant I could iterate on the ML pipeline without touching the main API.")
B.EB=s(["Sourcing accurate, up-to-date CDL questions across different state DMV variants.","Designing a progress algorithm that identifies weak areas and prioritizes them in review sessions.","Caching large question banks efficiently without bloating local storage."],t.s)
B.zg=new A.oI("CDL exam prep resources are scattered, expensive, or outdated. Most apps lack offline support, forcing drivers \u2014 who are often on the road \u2014 to be internet-dependent when studying between routes.","CDL A to Z bundles a complete question bank, study guides, and smart progress tracking into a single offline-capable app. A Node/MongoDB backend serves content updates, while the Flutter frontend caches questions locally for road-ready studying.","Flutter with BLoC for state management. Questions and study material are fetched from a Node.js REST API backed by MongoDB, then cached locally. Firebase handles push notifications for daily study reminders. Offline-first architecture ensures full functionality without connectivity.",B.EB,"Content quality matters as much as code quality for study apps. I spent significant time verifying question accuracy against official DMV materials. The adaptive review feature was the most impactful addition \u2014 users who used it passed at a meaningfully higher rate.")
